  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services for the flood -affected
people in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) assistance to vulnerable communities affected by floods in the Chattogram Division. This UNICEF project provides households in 4 districts with to sufficient quantities and quality of water to meet their domestic needs and access to safely managed sanitation services. This will be achieved through constructing new water supply systems and climate-resilient latrines. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 72,250 people, of whom 19,291 are women, 19,003 are men, and 33,956 are children. 2,022 people with disabilities also benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
